# CODEOWNERS — who is automatically asked to review changes to which files.
#
# Two developers, both named directly. With "required approvals: 1" on the main
# ruleset, the other person already reviews everything; this file only adds the
# paths where the WRONG person reviewing would be a real loss, so that a review
# request is raised automatically for them.
#
# On this public repository CODEOWNERS is enforced by the ruleset. If a third
# person ever joins, revisit — see ops/github-setup.md in the docs repository.

# Default: either developer may review anything.
*                               @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hot files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# components/polilingo.tsx (41 KB) was split into per-area modules under
# components/ in #12, so the hot-file protocol no longer applies to it.
# app/globals.css was split the same way: it now only imports the ordered
# partials under app/styles/, where the rules live. Both stay listed - the
# partials are the design system, and their order is the cascade, so a change
# to either affects every screen.

/app/globals.css                @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006
/app/styles/                    @muhammaduzair11 @junaidaslam2006

